%% MEETING INSTRUCTIONS FOR ATTENDEES
\section{Meeting Instructions for Unit Owners}

\noindent
\textbf{ {{ association_name | tex_escape }} }\\
\textbf{ {{ meeting_year }} Annual Meeting --- Instructions for Attendees}

\vspace{0.5em}

\subsection*{Before the Meeting}

\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.1em]
    \item \strong{Review this packet.} Read the notice, agenda, and any proposed resolutions carefully
    before the meeting.

    {% if election.election_required %}
    \item \strong{Review candidates.} Candidate biographical sketches are included in this packet.
    You may vote in person at the meeting or submit a proxy to designate how your vote should be cast.
    {% endif %}

    \item \strong{Submit your proxy (if not attending).} If you cannot attend in person, please complete
    and return the proxy form included in this packet to ensure your unit's vote is represented.
    {% if meeting.proxy_deadline %}
    \textbf{Proxy deadline: {{ meeting.proxy_deadline | format_date }}.}
    {% endif %}

    \item \strong{Review the financial documents.} The financial summary is included. Detailed financial
    records are available for inspection by appointment with management.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{At the Meeting}

\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.1em]
    \item \strong{Sign in.} Please sign the attendance and registration sheet upon arrival.
    {% if meeting.registration_time %}
    Registration opens at \textbf{ {{ meeting.registration_time }} }.
    {% endif %}

    \item \strong{Quorum.} The meeting will begin once quorum is confirmed. Quorum requires the
    presence, in person or by proxy, of owners representing
    {% if meeting.quorum_threshold %}
    \textbf{ {{ meeting.quorum_threshold }}\% } of the total votes.
    {% else %}
    the minimum number of votes required by the governing documents.
    {% endif %}
    If quorum is not present when the meeting is called to order, the chair will announce
    adjournment procedures.

    \item \strong{One vote per unit.} Each unit is entitled to one vote. If a unit has multiple
    owners, they collectively cast one vote.

    \item \strong{Decorum.} The meeting is conducted under the authority of the presiding officer.
    Please be courteous and allow each speaker to finish. Questions and comments are heard during
    the designated portions of the agenda.

    \item \strong{New Business.} Items of new business may be raised during the New Business portion
    of the agenda. Action on new business items is subject to quorum and procedural requirements.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{Proxy Holders}

\noindent
If you are serving as a proxy holder for another unit owner:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.1em]
    \item Bring the signed proxy form to the meeting.
    \item Present it to the registration desk upon arrival.
    \item Vote according to any specific directions given on the proxy form, or as you see fit if
    no specific direction is given.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{After the Meeting}

\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.1em]
    \item \strong{Minutes.} Meeting minutes will be prepared and distributed to all unit owners
    within the time required by the governing documents.

    {% if jx.org_meeting_after_annual %}
    \item \strong{Organizational Meeting.} The Board will hold its Organizational Meeting immediately
    following the Annual Meeting to elect officers. Unit owners are welcome to observe.
    {% endif %}

    \item \strong{Contact information.}
    For questions about this packet or the Annual Meeting, contact
    {% if management_contact %}\textbf{ {{ management_contact | tex_escape }} }{% else %}the Association's management{% endif %}
    {% if management_email %}at \texttt{ {{ management_email | tex_escape }} }{% endif %}
    {% if management_phone %}or {{ management_phone | tex_escape }}{% endif %}.
\end{itemize}
